![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When validating expected array fields, if a field is present but has an invalid type, we should record an explicit invalid-type diagnostic, process it as an empty array to prevent TypeErrors during execution, and continue processing in a fail-closed manner. Let's add explicit checks to verify that `reveal_eligibility_states`, `event_receipt_model`, `source_artifacts`, and `fixtures` are actual arrays when they are present, and default them to empty arrays if they are not.

```javascript
  const errors = [];
  if (!isRecord(policy)) errors.push('policy_record_required');
  if (!isRecord(fixtures)) errors.push('fixtures_record_required');
  if (!isRecord(inputs)) errors.push('inputs_record_required');
  if (errors.length > 0) {
    return failResult(errors);
  }

  let revealEligibilityStates = policy.reveal_eligibility_states;
  if (revealEligibilityStates !== undefined && !Array.isArray(revealEligibilityStates)) {
    errors.push('reveal_eligibility_states_invalid_type');
    revealEligibilityStates = [];
  }
  let eventReceiptModel = policy.event_receipt_model;
  if (eventReceiptModel !== undefined && !Array.isArray(eventReceiptModel)) {
    errors.push('event_receipt_model_invalid_type');
    eventReceiptModel = [];
  }
  let sourceArtifacts = policy.source_artifacts;
  if (sourceArtifacts !== undefined && !Array.isArray(sourceArtifacts)) {
    errors.push('source_artifacts_invalid_type');
    sourceArtifacts = [];
  }
  let fixturesList = fixtures.fixtures;
  if (fixturesList !== undefined && !Array.isArray(fixturesList)) {
    errors.push('fixtures_invalid_type');
    fixturesList = [];
  }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When validating expected array fields, if a field is present but has an invalid type, record an explicit invalid-type diagnostic and continue processing in a fail-closed manner.
2. When validating expected array fields in input data, if a field is present but is not an array, record a validation failure (blocker) and process it as an empty array. This prevents TypeErrors during execution while ensuring the system fails closed.
</details>

