1. Include fail-closed regression test cases in unit tests to verify that validation functions fail closed gracefully with specific errors when passed null, malformed, or non-record inputs.
2. When writing unit tests for package validators, assert the exact list of expected check IDs, verify they are emitted in strict byte-order, and ensure all checks pass.
